<article class="env-corollary" id="158825">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/158825">Corollary <span data-tag="158825">6.3.1.8</span>.</a> For every simplicial set $S$, there is a canonical bijection </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  [ S, \LGeom ] \simeq [ S^{op}, \RGeom ] \]
</div>
  <p> where $[K, \calC ]$ denotes the collection of equivalence classes of objects of $\Fun (K,\calC )$. In particular, $\LGeom $ and $\RGeom ^{op}$ are canonically isomorphic in the homotopy category of $\infty $-categories. </p>
</article>
<article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      According to Proposition <a href="/tag/B1A74B" data-tag="B1A74B">6.3.1.7</a>, both $[S, \LGeom ]$ and $[S^{op}, \RGeom ]$ can be identified with the collection of equivalence classes of topos fibrations $X \rightarrow S$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>